    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d175">

                <pb facs="0446" n="411" xml:id="pg411"/>

                <head>175. Memorandum From the Presidentʼs Special Assistant (Rostow) to President
                        Johnson<anchor n="1" xml:id="d175-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1966-05-10T19:45:00-04:00">May 10, 1966, 7:45 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline></opener>
                <p>[<hi rendition="#italic">less than 1 line of source text not declassified</hi>]
                    has supplied us with the first partial results of the Dominican Republic poll.
                    It covers a sample of 600 out of the 1,000 planned.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d175-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>The sample includes the whole of the DR except the towns of Santiago and Santo
                    Domingo; that is, it covers 60% of the potential voting population.</p>
                <p>The comparison with the March poll follows: <table cols="3" rows="6">
                        <row>
                            <cell/>
                            <cell>
                                <hi rendition="#italic">March 1966</hi>
                            </cell>
                            <cell>
                                <hi rendition="#italic">May 1966</hi>
                            </cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell> Balaguer </cell>
                            <cell role="num">54.8</cell>
                            <cell role="num">46.1</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell> Bosch </cell>
                            <cell role="num">19.2</cell>
                            <cell role="num">34.8</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>Bonnelly</cell>
                            <cell role="num">3.0</cell>
                            <cell role="num">5.2</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>Other</cell>
                            <cell role="num">1.4</cell>
                            <cell>—</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>Undecided</cell>
                            <cell role="num">21.6</cell>
                            <cell role="num">13.9</cell>
                        </row>
                    </table>
                </p>
                <p>To the question: Whom do you expect to win?, the answer was: <list>
                        <item> Bosch—36.4</item>
                        <item> Balaguer—31.7</item>
                        <item>Bonnelly—1.5</item>
                        <item>Donʼt know—30.4</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>[<hi rendition="#italic">less than 1 line of source text not declassified</hi>]
                    comments as follows: <list>
                        <label>a.</label>
                        <item> Balaguer should do well in Santiago; but he is weak in Santo
                            Domingo.</item>
                        <label>b.</label>
                        <item>In general, it looks like a horse race.</item>
                        <label>c.</label>
                        <item>He is mildly encouraged by the fact that the differences between voter
                            preferences and voter estimate of who will win does not indicate a
                            landslide mentality.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>I underlined again that nothing should be spared which will not be
                    counterproductive to get out the rural vote.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Walt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d175-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d175-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Johnson Library, National Security File, Intelligence File, Dominican
                    Republic Elections—1966. Top Secret; Eyes Only; Sensitive. An “L” on the
                    memorandum indicates the President saw it.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d175-f2" n="2" xml:id="d175-f2-content">
                <p>In a May 11 memorandum to the President, Rostow summarized the “unweighted full”
                    Dominican Republic poll results as follows: “Balaguer 43%, Bosch 37%, Bonnelly
                    4%, and Undecided 16%.” (Ibid.)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
